HST Office: closing a document window never releases the SolarMutex in the middle of its dispose.

HstRibbonBanner::dispose detaches its core (vcl/source/control/HstBannerCore.cxx). Core::Detach used to join
the banner's worker threads inside a SolarMutexReleaser, so the main thread could run a posted Resize of the
border window that was being disposed (SIGSEGV in ImplBorderWindow::Resize, null mpBorderView; seen when an
nd30 document was closed over UNO). The workers keep the core alive and check Detached() under the
SolarMutex before they post, so Detach no longer waits: it hands the threads to a list that a posted event
joins from the main loop, outside any dispose, and DeInitVCL joins what is left
(hst::banner::JoinDetachedWorkers, with the SolarMutex released as for the async event notifiers).

